  "generated_text": "1. We are given a right triangle \\( \\triangle XYZ \\) with \\( \\angle XYZ = 90^\\circ \\).\n2. The length of the hypotenuse \\( XZ \\) is given as \\( 12\\sqrt{2} \\).\n3. Since \\( \\angle XYZ = 45^\\circ \\), \\( \\triangle XYZ \\) is an isosceles right triangle.\n4. In an isosceles right triangle, the legs are equal, and the hypotenuse is \\( \\sqrt{2} \\) times the length of each leg.\n5. Let \\( XY = a \\).\n6. Therefore, \\( XZ = a\\sqrt{2} = 12\\sqrt{2} \\).\n7. Solving for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   a\\sqrt{2} = 12\\sqrt{2}\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by \\( \\sqrt{2} \\):\n   \\[\n   a = 12\n   \\]\n8. Since \\( XY = a \\):\n   \\[\n   XY = 12\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length \\( XY \\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
